{"name":"Bistro Napkin","hex":"#ece3dc","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bistro","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small casual restaurant or pub, typically serving French-style cuisine."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To eat at a bistro."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bistro"},{"term":"napkin","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A serviette; a (usually rectangular) piece of cloth or paper used at the table for wiping the mouth and hands for cleanliness while eating.","A nappy (UK), a diaper (American)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/napkin"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bistro","blocks":[{"text":"A bistro or bistrot, in its original Parisian form, is a small restaurant serving moderately priced, simple meals in a modest setting."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Jean_B%C3%A9raud_Au_Bistro.jpg/330px-Jean_B%C3%A9raud_Au_Bistro.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bistro","wikidata":"Q866742"},{"title":"Napkin","blocks":[{"text":"A napkin, serviette or face towelette is a square of cloth or paper tissue used at the table for wiping of the mouth and fingers while eating. It is also sometimes used as a bib by tucking it into a shirt collar. It is usually small and folded, sometimes in intricate designs, colors, and shapes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Napkin_ring.jpg/330px-Napkin_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Napkin","wikidata":"Q848532"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Bistro%21.jpg/500px-Bistro%21.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Bistro%21.jpg/1280px-Bistro%21.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&